{{intro|
Secure Mount Options for better Security Hardening / /etc/fstab modifications by a Linux distribution

Considering the most maintainable, stable solution. See also [[Dev/maintainability]] and [[Stable Version User Experience]].

'''Status:''' The chosen mechanism is <code>remount-secure</code>: a single systemd oneshot that remounts directories securely at boot (see [[#Default Mount Option Policy]], [[#Relationship to pam_namespace]] and [[#Towards Write-xor-Execute (W^X)]]). It touches no <code>/etc/fstab</code>, so it covers Qubes and non-Qubes uniformly. No generator and no second mechanism are used, to avoid competing mount operations. The alternative approaches enumerated below are retained for design rationale.

See also:

* [[Security-misc#Remount_Secure|Remount Secure]]
* [[noexec|Enhanced Security via Mount Options and Compiler Restrictions]]
}}
